name: sim.adjustView
description: Adjusts parameters of a view
luaSynopsis: int res = sim.adjustView(int viewHandleOrIndex, int objectHandle, int options, string viewLabel = None)
pythonSynopsis: int res = sim.adjustView(int viewHandleOrIndex, int objectHandle, int options, string viewLabel = nil)
inputs:
1. viewHandleOrIndex: handle of the view (can also be a floating view), or the index of the view.
2. objectHandle: handle of the object that you wish to associate with the view. Must be a viewable object. Can also be -1, in which case the view is emptied
3. options: bit-coded:
    - bit0-bit5= 0
    - bit6 (64) set=floating view is removed at simulation end
    - bit7 (128) set=floating view is ignored during a scene save operation
    - bit8 (256) set=the view is not modified. The return value of the function indicates if the view still exists (2), or does not exist anymore (1). No error is generated.
    - bit9 (512) set=the view is not modified. The return value of the function represents the object associated with the view.
4. viewLabel: a label that will be displayed at the top of a floating view. If None/nil is specified, then the name of the associated viewable object is taken as label.
outputs:
1. res: a value >0 in case of success
